{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/143772-the-mythwardens-a-changeling-the-lost-entitlement","id":143772,"title":"The Mythwardens - A Changeling: the Lost Entitlement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-20T12:12:56-07:00","id":143772,"title":"The Mythwardens - A Changeling: the Lost Entitlement","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#435459\"><span style=\"font-family:ProximaNova-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">I just rediscovered this entitlement I'd been working on a few months back, only to remember that I never finished it. The entitlement's privilege is still up in the air. I'd appreciate any constructive feedback or input you've got. =)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> The Mythwardens - A Changeling: the Lost Entitlement</b><br /> <br /> <i>It's not Disneyfication. It's insurance</i>.<br /> <br /> They censor school libraries, pressure television networks, and protest loudly outside feature films. They even make certain works of art disappear before they're ever shown and use blackmail, dreaming, and pledges to make sure they're never recreated. All the while, they foster new children's shows, inspire authors, and work to promote kinder stories about the magic beneath the world. Unlike most mortals, they don't do these things because they are personally offended, desperate to maintain children's innocence, or because they are naive. It's not about promoting a deity or preventing the world from going to hell in a hand-basket, either. Well, usually.<br /> <br /> No, the Mythwardens engage in their crusade because they know that stories have power, particularly the more they are told and watered with the swooning emotions of the young. Modern myths come in many forms and are shared by more people than ever before, locking stories and characters into particular shapes but giving them great influence. These changelings know that the real world affects the dream realms, and that the spread of terrible images can lead to very real manifestations in the Hedge. They believe that many Keepers of old are being maintained and given access to the world through mass media that reflects them - and that new Keepers are being spawned more easily and in worse forms because of media influence.<br /> <br /> The good news is that dangerous content can be changed, destroyed, and hidden by those who are on the lookout for the worst offenses. Better still, the promotion of kinder images of magic and stories of weaker fairies can shape the fae, if not across the world then in areas where those ideas really take root. The Mythwardens believe that with enough exposure and repetition, they can affect Keepers' powers and frailties, giving changelings real advantages when fighting back. Many believe that they create legendary weapons to fight the fae through popular fantasy films. Ultimately, the Mythwardens view the pruning and tending of public stories to be an extension of talecrafting and a way of making the world safer for humanity.<br /> <br /> Although there have always been censors, this order of changelings came into being with the mass-produced entertainments of the Victorian era. Mythwardens are often popular with mortals who have their own agendas for censoring art and can have powerful allies in parents' groups and slick politicians, but at times the order is reviled and fought by changelings who find their goals dubious and their tactics despicable.<br /> <br /> <b>Titles</b>: Mythwarden is the standard title, though some prefer Talewarden because of their mastery of Talecrafting.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Wyrd 3, Expression 3, Intimidation or Persuasion 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mien</b>: Mythwardens' true features will sporadically seem pixelated, blotted out, or otherwise obscured. They do not in fact vanish or become completely unrecognizable, and the shifts are brief enough that they confer no protection from being recognized by other changelings. Given their different approaches to their duties, there is no single Mythwarden uniform or style of dress. Those who work to steal horrific artworks before they're shown will dress appropriately, while those who work with the local PTA to remove certain books from the library will probably look like the other parents.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: The explosion of penny dreadfuls, fairy tales, and other bizarre elements in the Victorian era were of concern to some changelings, who vowed to study the effects of such fare on mortal dreams and local fae activity. They discovered that the most popular bogeys became real in some way, either by showing up as nightmare spawn, Hedge beasts, or manifesting in the traits of Keepers. There are some who believe that figures like Sweeney Todd fermented in the minds of Englishmen until their terror birthed Jack the Ripper, a monster that continues on as an immortal creature fed by the Ripper legend. While small circles of like-minded changelings had come together around these suspicions earlier, it was the Ripper's appearance that birthed the order as a proper entity; by the end of 1888, their vow was sealed.<br /> <br /> Modern Mythwardens often come from the ranks of parents, grandparents, teachers, and artists, and though there are more middle-class members than ever before, wealthier changelings are more common among the ranks. These are the people who either see the power of tales first-hand or have the luxury of pausing to consider how fiction affects fact. A few Mythwardens also pursue the order's duties out of religiously-based beliefs, searching for the word of God as it is reflected in the Hedge, Arcadia, and dreams, and casting out evil to protect the faithful.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization</b>: The Mythwardens are organized in circles, with a Master Warden at the heart of each one. This changeling has the most experience not only with recognizing myths that are worth meddling with, but also with handling them by various means. The Master Warden's duty is to delegate work, however, rather than taking it on directly; she is supposed to keep an eye on larger trends and threats while giving lesser members the leads and new apprentices. Some circles have and encourage members that are highly specialized in a medium (such as television), a myth type (such as monster stories), or a method (such as blackmail).<br /> <br /> Concepts: former parent, movie reviewer, pop psychologist, nightmare specialist, blackmailer, dutiful defender, talecrafting specialist (or addict).<br /> <br /> <b>Privileges</b><br /> <br /> Fully initiated Mythwardens enjoy the following privilege:<br /> <br /> <b>Rumors About the Mythwardens</b><br /> <br /> Some fear that the Mythwardens are actually searching for the best terrors mortals can dream up and then keeping those nightmares for themselves, to be unleashed at a later date, possibly in a violent takeover. Proof of any storage of monstrous ideas would be damning to the sect, which has always claimed to destroy the dangers it finds.<br /> <br /> Others believe that the Mythwardens are either deliberately or accidentally softening up humanity through their efforts, making people less likely to recover from encounters with the Fae and other ugliness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T17:06:41-07:00","id":148263,"title":"","content":"Looks pretty good. The mein seems a little odd if they are supposed to have been around since Jack the Ripper times.<br /> Some suggestions for Privileges. One for a token, one for goblin contract. Pretty powerful as they stand. To tone them down you can make the token only work on art pieces, make it resistible to remember the original, or change the drawback so it only lasts for one day before having to pay more glamour. For contract you can make it limited to one scene (though I'd get rid of the willpower dot cost then), up glamour cost, or make the frailty random/up to the ST.<br /> <br /> Censor<br /> <br /> Upon initiation the new Mythwarden is given a Censor. A censor can be anything that burns. An actual censor, a firework sparkler, a stick of incense, a lantern, a torch, a lighter. However, whatever form the Censor takes, it will not burn. Instead it produces nothing but black smoke. By waving the Censor over something with a narrative, a changeling is able to cleanse it of &quot;evil&quot;. Generally the Wardens use this on this like books, scripts, DVDs, CDs, and so on but it could include things as esoteric as camera footage, police reports or more.The changeling is able to rewrite the &quot;darker&quot; elements within a piece, though the quality of the rewrite might be subject to an Expression roll. Murder, death, torture and cussing are changed to more acceptable things. At the very least, they are done off screen or made ambiguous. All will accept the alterations as the original work.<br /> <br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Mein: It varies. However, whatever form the Censor takes, it's smoke turns white and a shining blue flame ignites, so long as Censor remains active.<br /> <br /> Drawback: The change is not permanent. After one week the art reverts to it's original state. A changeling can extend this duration by expending more glamour. One glamour for the first week, two for the second and so on. It soon become impossible to maintain for all but the most powerful of changelings.<br /> <br /> Catch: To use without glamour a character must have first convinced the maker of the piece that their alterations are better than the original narrative.<br /> <br /> <br /> Inflict Frality<br /> <br /> The Mythwarden is able to bind the stories of Fairie failures into other beings. However, doing so also compels them to those restrictions.<br /> <br /> Cost: 3 Glamour + 1 Willpower dot<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Expression + Wyrd - Resolve + Wyrd<br /> <br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Catch: The changeling has made and distributed a significant work (film, book, epic poem, ect) about the target and included the intended frailty within.<br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> Dramtic Failure: The Mythwarden gains a minor frailty but nothing else in return.<br /> Failure: The contract fails.<br /> Success: The character and their target gain a minor frailty permanently. The Mythwarden chooses the frailty of their target but has no control over the weakness they gain.<br /> Exceptional Success: The target gains a major frailty instead of a minor one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2290,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","user":"TrickyBoots","date":". 05-25-2014, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","name":"TrickyBoots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T23:40:12-07:00","id":148436,"title":"","content":"I like the Censor power; I'd tone it down in that it only works on that particular copy (though it may be used on whole piles of the same book without penalty). You still have to convince people to use your version instead of the original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T02:16:21-07:00","id":148540,"title":"","content":"So, they are the counterpart of the Scarecrows. Nice.<br /> Besides, they are right. The True Fae lack of imagination or creativity, so they usually adapt from humanity\u00b4s. Better not giving them &quot;funny&quot; ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 05-25-2014, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T11:23:16-07:00","id":148805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/143772-the-mythwardens-a-changeling-the-lost-entitlement?p=148436#post148436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Censor power; I'd tone it down in that it only works on that particular copy (though it may be used on whole piles of the same book without penalty). You still have to convince people to use your version instead of the original.</div> </div> </div> </div>Permanent Frailties are also an issue even on Exceptional success because you can't remove them in any form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T09:56:54-07:00","id":150451,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for your thoughts!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mein seems a little odd if they are supposed to have been around since Jack the Ripper times. </div> </div> </div>I can see why the first descriptor would seem strange that way, but pixelation is probably the most recent development; otherwise, &quot;pixelated, blotted out, or otherwise obscured&quot; could show up a number of ways.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Censor<br /> <br /> Upon initiation the new Mythwarden is given a Censor. A censor can be anything that burns. An actual censor, a firework sparkler, a stick of incense, a lantern, a torch, a lighter. However, whatever form the Censor takes, it will not burn. Instead it produces nothing but black smoke. By waving the Censor over something with a narrative, a changeling is able to cleanse it of &quot;evil&quot;. Generally the Wardens use this on this like books, scripts, DVDs, CDs, and so on but it could include things as esoteric as camera footage, police reports or more.The changeling is able to rewrite the &quot;darker&quot; elements within a piece, though the quality of the rewrite might be subject to an Expression roll. Murder, death, torture and cussing are changed to more acceptable things. At the very least, they are done off screen or made ambiguous. All will accept the alterations as the original work.<br /> <br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Mein: It varies. However, whatever form the Censor takes, it's smoke turns white and a shining blue flame ignites, so long as Censor remains active.<br /> <br /> Drawback: The change is not permanent. After one week the art reverts to it's original state. A changeling can extend this duration by expending more glamour. One glamour for the first week, two for the second and so on. It soon become impossible to maintain for all but the most powerful of changelings.<br /> <br /> Catch: To use without glamour a character must have first convinced the maker of the piece that their alterations are better than the original narrative. </div> </div> </div>I like this token, thematically and otherwise! I would specify that the changeling must have read or otherwise studied the whole thing first, so they know what should be changed, and I would definitely tie it to an Expression roll. I don't know that I would extend its powers to police reports though, since that goes beyond the scope of what the entitlement is truly about. I like the catch quite a bit, though I'm wondering how the changes can really catch on if the results aren't permanent. Hmmm...<br /> <br /> Since frailties are permanent and such an inherent part of fae nature that not even the Others get to choose their own, I hesitate to put that sort of power in the hands of a changeling, though I can see where you were coming from with it. This does get me thinking of a talecrafting option which allows a changeling who successfully pulls it off to twist something from the original art to their own ends (like giving a replica of the hero's sword real power, or making the villain of the tale so much like the Whispering Widow that the Other will suffer from a penalty based on what the audience now believes to be her weakness). I've got more thinking to do!<br /> <br /> Thank you again!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T02:41:36-07:00","id":158857,"title":"","content":"Perhaps rather than Inflict Frailty being a contract, it could be a part of the censor. Any creatures/nightmares/etc. that are spawned from the work in question will automatically have at least one frailty inflicted as appropriate to the changed story. The longer the changes are in place, the more powerful the frailty will become(or the more other frailties that begin to be inflicted) Rather than fully sanitizing the works, they poison them instead in order to gain the advantage over their foes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}